lisa-design:
- The by-component subtree lock is now SELF-ENFORCING on the derivation path:
  resyncLeverageSatisfaction takes lockByComponentSubtreeWrite itself, so the three writers that
  derive through it (satisfied CREATE, satisfied DELETE, Subscribe) cannot forget it. Advisory locks
  are re-entrant within a transaction, so those callers still take it explicitly and EARLIER — to
  cover their own inserts/deletes as well as the derivation — at zero cost. ReAttest derives inline
  and so its explicit lock is load-bearing on its own. Do NOT delete the lock from
  resyncLeverageSatisfaction as "redundant": it is what makes partial adoption structurally
  impossible, and this invariant has been half-missed twice.
- TestEveryLeverageSatisfactionWriterTakesTheSubtreeLock (subtree_lock_invariant_test.go) pins it
  structurally via go/ast, because the lock is a Postgres advisory lock and a no-op under the sqlite
  unit driver — no unit test can observe the race it prevents. Verified the guard actually fails when
  the lock is removed from Subscribe.

lisa-addressed:
Human review round 4 (gusfcarvalho, PR #456) — 1 finding, valid, fixed:
- [Medium] Subscribe still didn't take lockByComponentSubtreeWrite: the previous commit added it to
  ReAttest but not Subscribe, WHILE rewriting the lock's doc to enumerate Subscribe as one of the
  four writers and to declare partial adoption "worse than useless" — so the comment asserted an
  invariant the code violated, which is exactly the failure mode it warns about. And I resolved the
  thread. Reachable case is worse than it looks: findOrCreateByComponent REUSES an existing
  by-component, and resyncLeverageSatisfaction rewrites the satisfaction of EVERY link inherited on
  it, so a stale value from Subscribe corrupts a PRE-EXISTING link rather than the new one.
  FIXED: (a) Subscribe takes the lock in the item loop right after findOrCreateByComponent;
  (b) resyncLeverageSatisfaction now takes the lock ITSELF, so the invariant is enforced by
  construction on the derivation path instead of by everyone remembering;
  (c) TestEveryLeverageSatisfactionWriterTakesTheSubtreeLock pins all five writers via go/ast, and
  was verified to fail when Subscribe's lock is removed.
